    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0765" n="753" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg753"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Japan)/10–245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Acting Political Adviser in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>)<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d538-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-15T20:00:00-05:00">October 15, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Your 13, Oct 2. 1. The existence of diplomatic missions to the Japanese
                    Government is not deemed consistent with the purposes and character of allied
                    occupation of Japan or with the position of the occupying authorities.</p>
                <p>2. If it is so desired, neutral nations might designate a diplomatic agent or
                    representative of that character to maintain contact with the Headquarters of
                    the Supreme Commander for the Allies.</p>
                <p>3. The Japanese Government should be instructed that it should not carry on
                    relations with neutral governments except in accordance with such procedure as
                    may be established by SCAP.</p>
                <pb facs="0766" n="754" xml:id="pg754"/>
                <p>War Dept is informing SCAP as above.</p>
                <p>We feel that in light of foregoing Japanese diplomatic representatives abroad
                    should be recalled.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d538-f1" n="47" type="source" xml:id="d538-f1-content">
                <p>Substance reported to the Missions at Bern as 2989, at Lisbon as 1656, at Madrid
                    as 1728, and at Stockholm as 1933.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
